   "notes": "Cambridge Union Society (Waterhouse 1866), garden front facing the lawn off Bridge Street (x from the NE end). Polychrome red brick with stone bands: two-storey range of paired mullioned windows with colonnettes on the ground floor (x 0-15.5), then the twin-gabled entrance block with a pointed-arch doorway under a tall traceried two-light window and roundel (left gable) and a stone oriel over two ground-floor sashes (right gable). Wall identification (which face of the Union this is) inferred from geometry; tiled roof and gables not modelled. (length 24.1 m, height 10.2 m from walls.json)",
